{#
    Products grid — merchant-placeable.

    Unlike the other home components, the products are NOT rendered server-side:
    <falak-products-list> fetches them from /api/storefront and renders its own
    <falak-product-card> children. That keeps this section live without the
    merchant republishing — a price or stock change shows on the next page load,
    and the card stays the single definition of what a product looks like.

    The trade-off is deliberate and only acceptable here: the home page is not
    the page a shopper reaches from a product search, so the products being
    absent from the initial HTML costs nothing. The product listing page renders
    server-side for exactly the opposite reason.

    | Variable            | Type    | Description                             |
    | component.title     | ?string | section title, localized server-side    |
    | component.limit     | ?int    | how many products to show               |
    | component.columns   | ?string | grid density on desktop                 |
    | component.category  | ?string | category id; empty means all products   |
    | component.show_count| ?bool   | render the "showing N of M" line        |
    | position            | int     |                                         |

    Customizer bindings — full rules in README, "Customizer annotations".
    | Element         | Tag                      |
    | h2.block__title | data-falak-field="title" |

    The grid itself carries no binding: its fields are settings rather than
    text, and the platform already makes the whole component selectable.

    The `card` styleable role has no element: <falak-products-list> renders
    its own cards, so the role reaches them through the --falak-el-* custom
    properties, read back in app.css under "Customizer style hooks".
#}
<section class="block block--products" id="products-{{ position }}" {{ falak_section() }}>
    <div class="container">
        {% if component.title %}
            <h2 class="block__title" data-falak-field="title" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.title') }}">{{ component.title }}</h2>
        {% endif %}

        <falak-products-list
            limit="{{ component.limit|default(8) }}"
            columns="{{ component.columns|default(4) }}"
            {% if component.category %}category="{{ component.category }}"{% endif %}
            {% if component.show_count %}show-count{% endif %}
            {# Each card carries the platform add-to-cart button. #}
            card-button
            source="home.products"></falak-products-list>
    </div>
</section>
